# GigWork Backend — Cursor Rules

## TypeScript Philosophy — Keep It Simple

- Use plain object types, not complex generics
- No `<T>`, `<Record<K,V>>`, multiple union chains, or mapped types
- If a type needs more than 2 lines to define, split it into named types
- Use `type` not `interface` for data shapes
- Prefer explicit over inferred — name your return types on functions

### Allowed

```ts
type UserId = string
type UserRole = 'worker' | 'employer' | 'admin'
type UserStatus = 'pending' | 'active' | 'suspended' | 'banned'

type User = {
  id: UserId
  phone: string | null
  email: string | null
  role: UserRole
  status: UserStatus
  created_at: string
}
```

### Not Allowed

```ts
// Too complex — ban this style
type ApiResponse<T extends Record<string, unknown>> = {
  data: T extends Array<infer U> ? U[] : T
}
```

---

## File & Folder Structure

```
src/
  routes/         # Express/Fastify route files — one file per resource
  controllers/    # One function per endpoint, no business logic here
  services/       # All business logic lives here
  repositories/   # All DB queries live here — no raw SQL in services
  middlewares/    # auth, role check, validation, error handler
  validators/     # Zod schemas for every request body
  types/          # All shared type definitions — one file per domain
  utils/          # Pure helper functions only
  config/         # Env vars, DB config, constants
```

---

## API Response — Always Use This Shape

```ts
// types/api.ts
type ApiSuccess = {
  status: 'success'
  message: string
  data: object
}

type ApiError = {
  status: 'error'
  message: string
  errors: { field: string; message: string }[]
}

type ApiPaginated = {
  status: 'success'
  message: string
  data: object
  meta: {
    page: number
    limit: number
    total: number
    total_pages: number
  }
}
```

Every controller must call one of:

```ts
res.status(200).json(success(data, 'Profile created'))
res.status(400).json(error('Validation failed', fieldErrors))
res.status(200).json(paginated(items, total, page, limit))
```

